   130	Putting it all together — this paper presents ProveNFix, a static analyzer guided by temporal
   131	properties and supported by a proof-based repair strategy for fixing detected bugs where possible.
   132	Our goal is to automatically detect and fix bugs from some classes of program bugs and enable a
   133	modular and program-independent analysis/repair. An extensive evaluation shows that ProveNFix
   134	can fix various bug types, including null pointer dereferences, resource leak, and memory bugs. In
   135	total, ProveNFix detects 515 and repairs 492 bugs for a more than 1 million lines of code benchmark
   136	within 15 minutes, which outperforms SAVER and FootPatch regarding the execution time and
   137	fix rate. Besides, ProveNFix can fix other bugs, such as unchecked return values and customized
   138	temporal bugs. Our main contributions are summarized as follows:
   139	
